<title>USA: NASD fines Ill. firm for 'unfair' pricing of munis.</title>
<headline>NASD fines Ill. firm for 'unfair' pricing of munis.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>NASD said it fined Illinois-based Geneva Securities Inc $15,000 for selling municipal bonds to customers at &quot;unfair and unreasonable&quot; prices.</p>
<p>National Association of Securities Dealers also ordered a supervisor at the Schaumburg, Ill., firm to stop overseeing municipal brokers until the supervisor takes and passes a test to qualify for the job.</p>
<p>Leroy Messenger, chief operating officer of Geneva, was unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>--Vicky Stamas, 202-898-8314</p>
